{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype\\\\.unity|Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype\\\\.unity' Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md Tasks Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml Pipeline/Testing/README.md Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs | head -n 240\"","aggregated_output":"Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml:173:      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated in Section 5 Current Prototype Scene Evidence; confirmed present via Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity and Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity glob results.\"\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml:182:          \"requirement\": \"Scene-authoring work that changes objects generated or maintained through Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs must take exclusive-write locks on both that builder and Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\"\r\nPipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml:108:      \"resource_key\": \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nPipeline/Testing/README.md:7:`Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` is the sole authoritative Door Prototype scene. Its Unity asset identity is preserved by moving it together with `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.meta`.\r\nDocs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:233:- **Current prototype scene-builder lock:** scene-authoring work that changes objects generated or maintained through `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs` must take exclusive-write locks on both that builder and `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`. This specifically applies to doorway-crossing work that creates/configures the forward-side crossing trigger and, under the current scene-built UI approach, to final-victory work that creates/configures the **You Escaped** overlay. If a later approved architecture moves the overlay or another scene object into a separately owned runtime prefab/asset, the task may lock that actual asset instead; the task graph must reflect the implementation that exists when it is dispatched.\r\nDocs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:273:- `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` is the current canonical gameplay prototype scene and is the scene maintained by `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs`.\r\nDocs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:274:- `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` is a small non-canonical stub containing the default-style Main Camera and Directional Light; its camera is perspective, not the orthographic isometric gameplay camera. It must not be cited as an alternative implemented gameplay prototype.\r\nDocs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:327:- The required delivery target is a **Windows Standalone build**. The current canonical gameplay scene is `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`; that scene (or a later human-approved replacement canonical gameplay scene) must be registered in Unity Build Settings before the Windows delivery requirement can be considered complete. A committed `EditorBuildSettings.asset` with no registered canonical gameplay scene is confirmed incomplete build configuration and must remain represented as open configuration work. The top-level `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` and `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity` stubs do not satisfy this requirement merely because they are `.unity` files.\r\nTasks/NSC-019.yaml:22:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\r\nTasks/NSC-019.yaml:134:      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-009.yaml:20:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\r\nTasks/NSC-008.yaml:21:    \"unity-scene:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unit