{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md | sed -n '125,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"   125\tThe camera could now translate with the player while preserving a fixed isometric orientation.\r\n   126\t\r\n   127\t### Evaluation Pass 2 — Static Pass\r\n   128\t\r\n   129\tThe Evaluator again passed the implementation statically.\r\n   130\t\r\n   131\tI rebuilt and tested the scene in Unity again.\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\t### Unity Runtime Test 2 — Failure\r\n   134\t\r\n   135\tThe camera still did not frame the game correctly. The player-follow behavior existed, but the viewing side and framing were wrong and the starting door was no longer properly visible.\r\n   136\t\r\n   137\tI recorded this separately as:\r\n   138\t\r\n   139\t`Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json`\r\n   140\t\r\n   141\tRuntime feedback files are preserved as an append-only history:\r\n   142\t\r\n   143\t```text\r\n   144\truntime_feedback000.json\r\n   145\truntime_feedback001.json\r\n   146\truntime_feedback002.json\r\n   147\t...\r\n   148\t```\r\n   149\t\r\n   150\t### Implementation Pass 3 — Refiner Made No Progress\r\n   151\t\r\n   152\tThe Refiner reported `implemented`, but it made **no observed changes under `Assets/`**.\r\n   153\t\r\n   154\tThis exposed a weakness in the original Assignment 5 implementation contract: Assignment 5 expected an `implemented` result to always include modified files and would crash otherwise.\r\n   155\t\r\n   156\tFor Assignment 6, I changed that behavior. A no-op refinement is now treated as a **failed repair attempt**, not a pipeline error.\r\n   157\t\r\n   158\tThe GER progress guard detected the no-op and forced the loop to continue instead of accepting a false success.\r\n   159\t\r\n   160\t### Implementation Pass 4 — Final Refinement\r\n   161\t\r\n   162\tThe final allowed refinement modified the scene builder and its tests again. The Evaluator verified the current camera implementation and the additional regression safeguards.\r\n   163\t\r\n   164\tThe implementation now used:\r\n   165\t\r\n   166\t- orthographic projection,\r\n   167\t- a consistent isometric orientation,\r\n   168\t- camera translation/follow without free rotation,\r\n   169\t- stable camera-to-player offset behavior,\r\n   170\t- tests for camera framing and fixed rotation,\r\n   171\t- a regression check for invalid/null follow targets.\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\tThe Evaluator returned PASS.\r\n   174\t\r\n   175\tAt this point, all **three allowed refinements** had been used. If the feature had failed again, the Circuit Breaker would have escalated the task to human review.\r\n   176\t\r\n   177\t## Final Unity Validation\r\n   178\t\r\n   179\tAfter the final GER pass, I rebuilt the Door Prototype scene in Unity and tested the result manually.\r\n   180\t\r\n   181\tThe camera now behaves as intended: it uses a **Diablo / Ultima Online-style orthographic isometric presentation**, follows the player appropriately, and does not allow free camera rotation.\r\n   182\t\r\n   183\tI then ran the relevant Unity automated tests:\r\n   184\t\r\n   185\t- the full `DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests` EditMode suite;\r\n   186\t- the existing `DoorInteractionPlayModeTests` PlayMode suite.\r\n   187\t\r\n   188\t**All tests passed.**\r\n   189\t\r\n   190\t## Did the Pipeline Catch Something I Would Have Missed?\r\n   191\t\r\n   192\tYes.\r\n   193\t\r\n   194\tThe most useful result of this assignment was discovering that a static evaluator can prove that code satisfies a written requirement while the actual game can still be broken.\r\n   195\t\r\n   196\tThe first camera implementation passed static evaluation because it was orthographic and used a fixed isometric rotation. In Unity, however, it faced the wrong direction and did not follow the player.\r\n   197\t\r\n   198\tThe second implementation also passed static evaluation but still framed gameplay incorrectly.\r\n   199\t\r\n   200\tHuman Play Mode testing exposed those failures. The failures were converted into structured runtime feedback and fed back into GER so the Refiner could continue working on the same selected goal.\r\n   201\t\r\n   202\tThe pipeline also caught a different failure during Pass 3: the Refiner made no code changes even though unresolved runtime feedback existed. A GER progress guard rejected that no-op repair and counted it toward the Circuit Breaker instead of allowing the pipeline to fail silently.\r\n   203\t\r\n   204\t## Important Output Artifacts\r\n   205\t\r\n   206\tThe Assignment 6 run preserves the complete history of the experiment under:\r\n   207\t\r\n   208\t`Assignment6GER/outputs/`\r\n   209\t\r\n   210\tImportant artifacts include:\r\n   211\t\r\n   212\t```text\r\n   213\tger_contract.json\r\n   214\t\r\n   215\timplementation_pass_1.json\r\n   216\timplementation_pass_2.json\r\n   217\timplementation_pass_3.json\r\n   218\timplementation_pass_4.json\r\n   219\t\r\n   220\tevaluation_pass_1.json\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"better_next_step_if_any\":\"I’m tightening the final verdict around three disqualifying gaps: the recommended proof has an unexecutable human reset check, the new scoped-canon model can silently miss impacts, and the proposed write path has no enforcement mechanism. I’m also checking whether the two-repair budget and protected-main assumptions agree with the repository’s only real GER and branch evidence.\",\"failure_if_followed\":[\"A literal implementation could normalize removing a stale dependency from a contract until preflight passes, instead of resolving the authority conflict that made the dependency stale.\"],\"final_assessment\":\"synthesis_needs_revision\",\"hidden_assumptions\":[\"Two repairs are enough despite the only documented Unity GER consuming all three allowed refinements.\",\"A protected integration ref exists and is the frozen base, although `main` is eight commits behind frozen `provider-adapters` HEAD.\",\"The current PowerShell Unity runner is a bounded host service, although it waits on Unity without a process timeout or project-lock/import recovery.\"],\"ignored_minority_arguments\":[\"The Unity/workflow reviews called for an explicit Windows host, Editor-lock, import/cache, and worktree strategy; the synthesis falls back to the existing manual runner.\"],\"reason\":\"The high-level delivery-first correction is stronger than the current platform-first roadmap, but the exact minimal architecture and NSC-005 proof are under-specified at the points where authority and Unity side effects matter most.\",\"strongest_counter_case\":\"Use no new autonomous coordinator during the remaining window: resolve branch and scene authority first, freeze one human-approved micro-contract, let a directly supervised coding assistant work on an ordinary branch, invoke the existing clean Unity runner manually, perform human Play Mode review, and merge. Git commits are sufficient recovery until an actual repeated failure justifies a journal. Prefer a real integration slice such as NSC-003A—or a build-producing slice—over debug-only mana plumbing.\",\"synthesis_weaknesses\":[\"The proposed success check says a human approves reset behavior, but the repository has no reset orchestrator, debug reset control, or other Play Mode caller.\",\"NSC-005 adds no ready dependent by itself; both dependents remain blocked on several other tasks, so it does not test dependency satisfaction or readiness semantics.\"],\"what_would_change_my_mind\":[\"A concrete, reviewed write-containment design and executable Windows Unity-host path.\",\"A revised experiment that resolves canonical-scene and protected-ref authority before producing evidence.\"]}"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git rev-list --count main..HEAD\ngit rev-list --count HEAD..main\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py | sed -n '190,325p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/openai_codex.py | sed -n '80,115p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/claude_code.py | sed -n '95,125p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/Testing/run_unity_tests_clean.ps1 | sed -n '90,175p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git rev-list --count main..HEAD\ngit rev-list --count HEAD..main\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/contracts.py | sed -n '190,325p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/openai_codex.py | sed -n '80,115p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/claude_code.py | sed -n '95,125p'\nnl -ba Pipeline/Testing/run_unity_tests_clean.ps1 | sed -n '90,175p'\"","aggregated_output":"0\n   190\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n   191\tclass AgentInvocationRequest:\n   192\t    schema_version: str\n   193\t    run_id: str\n   194\t    role: str\n   195\t    prompt: str\n   196\t    context_paths: tuple[str, ...]\n   197\t    allowed_capabilities: tuple[str, ...]\n   198\t    write_boundaries: WriteBoundaries\n   199\t    output_schema: Mapping[str, Any]\n   200\t    model_capability_class: str\n   201\t    budgets: Budgets\n   202\t    provider_configuration_key: str\n   203\t\n   204\t    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n   205\t        if self.schema_version != AGENT_INVOCATION_REQUEST_SCHEMA_VERSION:\n   206\t            raise ContractValidationError(\n   207\t                \"unsupported AgentInvocationRequest schema_version\"\n   208\t            )\n   209\t        if not isinstance(self.run_id, str) or not _SLUG.fullmatch(self.run_id):\n   210\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"run_id must be a lowercase ASCII slug of 1..64 characters\")\n   211\t        if not isinstance(self.role, str) or not _IDENTIFIER.fullmatch(self.role):\n   212\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"role must be a conservative identifier\")\n   213\t        if not isinstance(self.prompt, str) or not self.prompt.strip():\n   214\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"prompt must be non-empty\")\n   215\t        try:\n   216\t            validate_text(self.prompt, path=\"prompt\")\n   217\t        except JsonValueError as exc:\n   218\t            raise ContractValidationError(str(exc)) from exc\n   219\t        object.__setattr__(\n   220\t            self,\n   221\t            \"context_paths\",\n   222\t            _path_tuple(self.context_paths, field=\"context_paths\"),\n   223\t        )\n   224\t        capabilities = _string_tuple(self.allowed_capabilities, field=\"allowed_capabilities\")\n   225\t        unknown = set(capabilities) - SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES\n   226\t        if unknown:\n   227\t            raise ContractValidationError(f\"unsupported capabilities: {sorted(unknown)}\")\n   228\t        object.__setattr__(self, \"allowed_capabilities\", capabilities)\n   229\t        if type(self.write_boundaries) is not WriteBoundaries:\n   230\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"write_boundaries has the wrong type\")\n   231\t        has_write = \"repository_write\" in capabilities\n   232\t        if has_write and not self.write_boundaries.allowed_paths:\n   233\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"repository_write requires at least one allowed path\")\n   234\t        if not has_write and (self.write_boundaries.allowed_paths or self.write_boundaries.denied_paths):\n   235\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"write paths require repository_write\")\n   236\t        if type(self.output_schema) not in (dict, MappingProxyType):\n   237\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"output_schema must be an exact JSON object\")\n   238\t        from .schema_validation import validate_schema\n   239\t\n   240\t        try:\n   241\t            schema_value = (\n   242\t                thaw_json(self.output_schema)\n   243\t                if isinstance(self.output_schema, MappingProxyType)\n   244\t                else self.output_schema\n   245\t            )\n   246\t            frozen_schema = freeze_json(schema_value, path=\"$.output_schema\")\n   247\t        except JsonValueError as exc:\n   248\t            raise ContractValidationError(str(exc)) from exc\n   249\t        try:\n   250\t            validate_schema(frozen_schema)\n   251\t        except Exception as exc:\n   252\t            from .schema_validation import SchemaValidationError\n   253\t            if isinstance(exc, SchemaValidationError):\n   254\t                raise ContractValidationError(str(exc)) from exc\n   255\t            raise\n   256\t        object.__setattr__(self, \"output_schema\", frozen_schema)\n   257\t        if self.model_capability_class not in MODEL_CAPABILITY_CLASSES:\n   258\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"unknown model_capability_class\")\n   259\t        if type(self.budgets) is not Budgets:\n   260\t            raise ContractValidationError(\"budgets has the wrong type\")\n   261\t        if (\n   262\t            not isinstance(self.provider_configuration_key, str)\n   263\t            or not _IDENTIFIER.fullmatch(self.provider_configuration_key)\n   264\t        ):\n   265\t            raise ContractValidationError(\n   266\t                \"provider_configuration_key must be a conservative identifier\"\n   267\t            )\n   268\t\n   269\t    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n   270\t        return {\n   271\t            \"schema_version\": self.schema_version,\n   272\t            \"run_id\": self.run_id,\n   273\t            \"role\": self.role,\n   274\t            \"prompt\": self.prompt,\n   275\t            \"context_paths\": list(self.context_paths),\n   276\t            \"allowed_capabilities\": list(self.allowed_capabilities),\n   277\t            \"write_boundaries\": WriteBoundaries.to_dict(self.write_boundaries),\n   278\t            \"output_schema\": thaw_json(self.output_schema),\n   279\t            \"model_capability_class\": self.model_capability_class,\n   280\t            \"budgets\": Budgets.to_dict(self.budgets),\n   281\t            \"provider_configuration_key\": self.provider_configuration_key,\n   282\t        }\n   283\t\n   284\t    @classmethod\n   285\t    def from_dict(cls, value: Mapping[str, Any]) -> \"AgentInvocationRequest\":\n   286\t        fields = {\n   287\t            \"schema_version\", \"run_id\", \"role\", \"prompt\", \"context_paths\", \"allowed_capabilities\",\n   288\t            \"write_boundaries\", \"output_schema\", \"model_capability_class\",\n   289\t            \"budgets\", \"provider_configuration_key\",\n   290\t        }\n   291\t        _expect_fields(value, fields, where=\"AgentInvocationRequest\")\n   292\t        return cls(\n   293\t            value[\"schema_version\"],\n   294\t            value[\"run_id\"],\n   295\t            value[\"role\"],\n   296\t            value[\"prompt\"],\n   297\t            value[\"context_paths\"],\n   298\t            value[\"allowed_capabilities\"],\n   299\t            WriteBoundaries.from_dict(value[\"write_boundaries\"]),\n   300\t            value[\"output_schema\"],\n   301\t            value[\"model_capability_class\"],\n   302\t            Budgets.from_dict(value[\"budgets\"]),\n   303\t            value[\"provider_configuration_key\"],\n   304\t        )\n   305\t\n   306\t    def is_path_writable(self, candidate: str) -> bool:\n   307\t        try:\n   308\t            path = validate_repository_path(candidate, field=\"candidate path\")\n   309\t        except ContractValidationError:\n   310\t            return False\n   311\t        if \"repository_write\" not in self.allowed_capabilities:\n   312\t            return False\n   313\t        parts = tuple(path.split(\"/\"))\n   314\t        folded_parts = tuple(part.casefold() for part in parts)\n   315\t\n   316\t        def prefix(boundary: str) -> bool:\n   317\t            boundary_parts = tuple(part.casefold() for part in boundary.split(\"/\"))\n   318\t            return folded_parts[:len(boundary_parts)] == boundary_parts\n   319\t        if any(prefix(item) for item in self.write_boundaries.denied_paths):\n   320\t            return False\n   321\t        return any(prefix(item) for item in self.write_boundaries.allowed_paths)\n   322\t\n   323\t\n   324\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n   325\tclass Usage:\n    80\t                return self._response(result, final_path)\n    81\t        except (ProviderFailure, ProviderOutputInvalid, ProviderTimeout,\n    82\t                ProviderRequestRejected, ProviderTransportError):\n    83\t            raise\n    84\t        except Exception as exc:\n    85\t            raise ProviderTransportError(\n    86\t                f\"Codex local temporary-file transport failed: {type(exc).__name__}\"\n    87\t            ) from exc\n    88\t\n    89\t    def _validate_request_policy(self, request: AgentInvocationRequest) -> None:\n    90\t        capabilities = frozenset(request.allowed_capabilities)\n    91\t        if capabilities & _FORBIDDEN_CAPABILITIES:\n    92\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\n    93\t                \"Codex does not support repository writing or approved command execution\"\n    94\t            )\n    95\t        if not capabilities <= _REPOSITORY_CAPABILITIES:\n    96\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\"Codex capability set is unsupported\")\n    97\t        if request.context_paths and not capabilities:\n    98\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\"Codex requires repository capability for context_paths\")\n    99\t        if capabilities and not self.externally_enforced_read_only_repository:\n   100\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\n   101\t                \"Codex repository access requires an explicit externally read-only profile\"\n   102\t            )\n   103\t        if request.budgets.token_limit is not None:\n   104\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\"Codex currently requires token_limit to be null\")\n   105\t\n   106\t    @staticmethod\n   107\t    def _validate_model(model: str) -> None:\n   108\t        if type(model) is not str or not model or model != model.strip():\n   109\t            raise ProviderTransportError(\"Codex requires a concrete configured model identifier\")\n   110\t\n   111\t    def _argv(self, model: str, schema_path: Path, final_path: Path) -> tuple[str, ...]:\n   112\t        return (\n   113\t            self.executable, \"exec\", \"--ephemeral\", \"--ignore-user-config\",\n   114\t            \"--ignore-rules\", \"--strict-config\", \"--skip-git-repo-check\",\n   115\t            \"--sandbox\", \"danger-full-access\", \"--model\", model,\n    95\t            raise\n    96\t        except Exception as exc:\n    97\t            raise ProviderTransportError(\n    98\t                f\"Claude Code temporary workspace setup failed: {type(exc).__name__}\"\n    99\t            ) from exc\n   100\t\n   101\t        return self._response_from_result(result)\n   102\t\n   103\t    @staticmethod\n   104\t    def _validate_request_policy(request: AgentInvocationRequest) -> None:\n   105\t        capabilities = frozenset(request.allowed_capabilities)\n   106\t        if capabilities & _FORBIDDEN_CAPABILITIES:\n   107\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\n   108\t                \"Claude Code does not support repository writing or command execution\"\n   109\t            )\n   110\t        if not capabilities <= _REPOSITORY_CAPABILITIES:\n   111\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\"Claude Code capability set is unsupported\")\n   112\t        if request.context_paths and not capabilities:\n   113\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\n   114\t                \"Claude Code requires a repository capability for context_paths\"\n   115\t            )\n   116\t        if request.budgets.token_limit is not None:\n   117\t            raise ProviderRequestRejected(\n   118\t                \"Claude Code currently requires token_limit to be null\"\n   119\t            )\n   120\t\n   121\t    @staticmethod\n   122\t    def _validate_model(model: str) -> None:\n   123\t        if (\n   124\t            type(model) is not str\n   125\t            or not model\n    90\t\r\n    91\t    $preStatus = Get-WorkingTreeStatus $repositoryRoot\r\n    92\t    if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($preStatus)) {\r\n    93\t        Write-Host \"Working tree paths present before test run:\"\r\n    94\t        Write-Host $preStatus\r\n    95\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitPrecondition \"PRECONDITION FAILURE: Git working tree must be completely clean, including untracked files.\"\r\n    96\t    }\r\n    97\t\r\n    98\t    $preHead = Invoke-Git $repositoryRoot @(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\r\n    99\t    $preTree = Invoke-Git $repositoryRoot @(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^{tree}\")\r\n   100\t    $versionLine = Get-Content -LiteralPath $projectSettings | Where-Object { $_ -match '^m_EditorVersion:\\s*(.+)$' } | Select-Object -First 1\r\n   101\t    if (-not $versionLine -or $versionLine -notmatch '^m_EditorVersion:\\s*(.+)$') {\r\n   102\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitPrecondition \"PRECONDITION FAILURE: Could not read m_EditorVersion from $projectSettings\"\r\n   103\t    }\r\n   104\t    $unityVersion = $Matches[1].Trim()\r\n   105\t\r\n   106\t    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($UnityExecutable)) {\r\n   107\t        $UnityExecutable = Join-Path ${env:ProgramFiles} \"Unity\\Hub\\Editor\\$unityVersion\\Editor\\Unity.exe\"\r\n   108\t    }\r\n   109\t    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $UnityExecutable -PathType Leaf)) {\r\n   110\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitPrecondition \"PRECONDITION FAILURE: Unity executable does not exist: $UnityExecutable\"\r\n   111\t    }\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t    $artifactDirectory = Join-Path ([System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) (\"NoSafeCircle-UnityTests-\" + [Guid]::NewGuid().ToString(\"N\"))\r\n   114\t    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $artifactDirectory | Out-Null\r\n   115\t    $xmlPath = Join-Path $artifactDirectory \"test-results.xml\"\r\n   116\t    $logPath = Join-Path $artifactDirectory \"unity.log\"\r\n   117\t    Write-Host \"Temporary artifacts will be preserved at: $artifactDirectory\"\r\n   118\t\r\n   119\t    $unityExitCode = $null\r\n   120\t    $invocationFailure = $null\r\n   121\t    $xmlPublished = $false\r\n   122\t    try {\r\n   123\t        $unityArguments = @(\r\n   124\t            \"-batchmode\",\r\n   125\t            \"-projectPath\", (ConvertTo-WindowsCommandLineArgument $resolvedProjectPath),\r\n   126\t            \"-runTests\",\r\n   127\t            \"-testPlatform\", (ConvertTo-WindowsCommandLineArgument $TestPlatform),\r\n   128\t            \"-testFilter\", (ConvertTo-WindowsCommandLineArgument $TestFilter),\r\n   129\t            \"-testResults\", (ConvertTo-WindowsCommandLineArgument $xmlPath),\r\n   130\t            \"-logFile\", (ConvertTo-WindowsCommandLineArgument $logPath)\r\n   131\t        )\r\n   132\t        $unityProcess = Start-Process -FilePath $UnityExecutable -ArgumentList $unityArguments -Wait -PassThru\r\n   133\t        $unityExitCode = $unityProcess.ExitCode\r\n   134\t\r\n   135\t        $xmlPublicationDeadline = [DateTime]::UtcNow.AddSeconds(5)\r\n   136\t        do {\r\n   137\t            $xmlPublished = Test-Path -LiteralPath $xmlPath -PathType Leaf\r\n   138\t            if (-not $xmlPublished -and [DateTime]::UtcNow -lt $xmlPublicationDeadline) {\r\n   139\t                Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 100\r\n   140\t            }\r\n   141\t        } while (-not $xmlPublished -and [DateTime]::UtcNow -lt $xmlPublicationDeadline)\r\n   142\t    }\r\n   143\t    catch {\r\n   144\t        $invocationFailure = $_.Exception.Message\r\n   145\t        $unityExitCode = -1\r\n   146\t    }\r\n   147\t    finally {\r\n   148\t        $postCheckFailure = $null\r\n   149\t        try {\r\n   150\t            $postHead = Invoke-Git $repositoryRoot @(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\r\n   151\t            $postTree = Invoke-Git $repositoryRoot @(\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD^{tree}\")\r\n   152\t            $postStatus = Get-WorkingTreeStatus $repositoryRoot\r\n   153\t        }\r\n   154\t        catch {\r\n   155\t            $postCheckFailure = $_.Exception.Message\r\n   156\t        }\r\n   157\t    }\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t    if ($postCheckFailure) {\r\n   160\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitMutation \"REPOSITORY CHECK FAILURE: Post-run Git checks could not complete: $postCheckFailure\"\r\n   161\t    }\r\n   162\t    if ($postHead -ne $preHead) {\r\n   163\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitMutation \"REPOSITORY MUTATION FAILURE: HEAD changed from $preHead to $postHead. No changes were restored.\"\r\n   164\t    }\r\n   165\t    if ($postTree -ne $preTree) {\r\n   166\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitMutation \"REPOSITORY MUTATION FAILURE: Git tree changed from $preTree to $postTree. No changes were restored.\"\r\n   167\t    }\r\n   168\t    if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($postStatus)) {\r\n   169\t        Write-Host \"Working tree paths changed or created during the test run:\"\r\n   170\t        Write-Host $postStatus\r\n   171\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitMutation \"REPOSITORY MUTATION FAILURE: Passing assertions plus a dirty repository is failure. No changes were restored.\"\r\n   172\t    }\r\n   173\t\r\n   174\t    if ($invocationFailure) {\r\n   175\t        Stop-WithCode $ExitUnity \"UNITY FAILURE: Unity could not be invoked: $invocationFailure`nXML: $xmlPath`nLog: $logPath\"\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
